# zoneadm — real-world examples

Administer Solaris/illumos zones (OS-level virtualization — the Solaris
cousin of containers). Pairs with `zonecfg`, which defines the zone.

## List and inspect

```sh
# List all zones with state, path, and brand
zoneadm list -cv

# Running zones only
zoneadm list -v
```

## Zone lifecycle

```sh
# Verify a zone's configuration before installing
zoneadm -z <zone_name> verify

# Install a zone
zoneadm -z <zone_name> install

# Boot a zone
zoneadm -z <zone_name> boot

# Reboot a zone
zoneadm -z <zone_name> reboot

# Halt a zone (hard stop)
zoneadm -z <zone_name> halt

# Graceful shutdown from the global zone
zoneadm -z <zone_name> shutdown
```

## Delete a zone

```sh
# Halt, uninstall, then remove the configuration
zoneadm -z <zone_name> halt
zoneadm -z <zone_name> uninstall
zonecfg -z <zone_name> delete
```

## Typical workflow

```sh
# Define with zonecfg, then verify/install/boot with zoneadm
zonecfg -z webzone create
zoneadm -z webzone verify
zoneadm -z webzone install
zoneadm -z webzone boot

# Log in to the new zone's console (exit with ~.)
zlogin -C webzone
```

## Subcommand reference

| Subcommand | Purpose |
|------------|---------|
| `list -cv` | all configured zones, verbose |
| `verify` | sanity-check config |
| `install` / `uninstall` | lay down / remove zone files |
| `boot` / `reboot` / `halt` | power control |
| `shutdown` | graceful stop |
| `attach` / `detach` | move zones between hosts |
